	<string>Tapeloop keeps the last minutes of your Mac's sound (for example the other side of a call) compressed in memory, so you can save it after it happened. Nothing is written to disk until you save.</string>
	<key>NSCalendarsFullAccessUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Tapeloop reads event titles to name your recordings and to offer saving a meeting that just ended. Nothing leaves this Mac.</string>
	<key>NSSpeechRecognitionUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Tapeloop transcribes saved recordings on this Mac, so you can read and search them.</string>
